ges-before\" data-recipe=\"3921\" data-servings=\"4\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">medium</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">zucchinis</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">sliced thin for maximum crispiness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a rich flavor and crunch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">grated Parmesan cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a cheesy goodness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">panko breadcrumbs</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for extra crunch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a hint of flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">enhances the overall taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">½</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a touch of warmth</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt and pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">season to your liking</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">as needed</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Cooking spray</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">helps achieve that perfect crisp</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3921-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3921\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Air Fryer&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the zucchini chips.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3921-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3921-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3921\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat your air fryer to 400°F (200°C). This ensures your zucchini chips will be perfectly crispy!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Wash and dry the zucchinis. Slice them into 1/8-inch thick rounds. The thinner, the crispier!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: In a bowl, mix together Parmesan, panko breadcrumbs, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, salt, and pepper. This mixture will add a delicious crunch!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Toss the zucchini slices with olive oil to coat them evenly. Then, dredge each slice in the breadcrumb mixture, pressing lightly to help it stick.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Place the coated zucchini slices in a single layer in the air fryer basket. Make sure they don’t overlap for even cooking!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Lightly spray the tops of the zucchini chips with cooking spray. Air-fry for 8–10 minutes, flipping halfway through, until they are golden brown and crispy.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3921-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Remove the chips from the air fryer and let them cool slightly. Serve immediately with your favorite dip. Enjoy your crispy creation!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3921-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>8g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbohydrates</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fiber</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to make your delicious air-fried zucchini chips!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Crispy-Air-Fried-Zucchini-Chips.webp\" alt=\"Fresh ingredients for Crispy Air-Fried Zucchini Chips displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-3919\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Crispy-Air-Fried-Zucchini-Chips.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Crispy-Air-Fried-Zucchini-Chips-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 medium <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">zucchinis</a></strong> – sliced thin for maximum crispiness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons olive oil</strong> – for a rich flavor and crunch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ cup grated Parmesan cheese</strong> – adds a cheesy goodness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ cup panko breadcrumbs</strong> – for extra crunch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon garlic powder</strong> – for a hint of flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ teaspoon onion powder</strong> – enhances the overall taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ teaspoon paprika</strong> – adds a touch of warmth</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt and pepper to taste</strong> – season to your liking</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cooking spray</strong> – helps achieve that perfect crisp</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-crispy-air-fried-zucchini-chips\"><strong>How to Make  Air-Fried Zucchini Chips</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready for a delightful snack! This recipe takes about 10 minutes to prepare and 8–10 minutes to cook. Let’s dive into making these crispy treats!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Preparation-Steps-for-Crispy-Air-Fried-Zucchini-Chips.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of Crispy Air-Fried Zucchini Chips, showcasing preheating the air fryer, slicing zucchinis, mixing the coating, and arranging the zucchini in the air fryer.\" class=\"wp-image-3920\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Preparation-Steps-for-Crispy-Air-Fried-Zucchini-Chips.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Preparation-Steps-for-Crispy-Air-Fried-Zucchini-Chips-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Air Fryer</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your air fryer to 400°F (200°C). This ensures your zucchini chips will be perfectly crispy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Zucchini</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Wash and dry the zucchinis. Slice them into 1/8-inch thick rounds. The thinner, the crispier!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Make the Coating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, mix together Parmesan, panko breadcrumbs, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, salt, and pepper. This mixture will add a delicious crunch!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Coat the Zucchini</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Toss the zucchini slices with olive oil to coat them evenly. Then, dredge each slice in the breadcrumb mixture, pressing lightly to help it stick.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Arrange in the Air Fryer</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the coated zucchini slices in a single layer in the air fryer basket. Make sure they don’t overlap for even cooking!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Spray and Cook</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Lightly spray the tops of the zucchini chips with cooking spray. Air-fry for 8–10 minutes, flipping halfway through, until they are golden brown and crispy.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the chips from the air fryer and let them cool slightly. Serve immediately with your favorite dip. Enjoy your crispy creation!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Snack</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>With your favorite dip</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-crispy-air-fried-zucchini-chips\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Air-Fried Zucchini Chips</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Slice zucchini thinly for maximum crispiness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pat the slices dry to remove excess moisture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with seasonings like garlic powder or paprika.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t overcrowd the air fryer basket for even cooking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Check frequently to avoid overcooking and ensure perfect crunch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-crispy-air-fried-zucchini-chips\"><strong>How to Serve this Air-Fried Zucchini Chips</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with a zesty yogurt dip for a refreshing twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with homemade salsa for a crunchy snack.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy alongside a creamy avocado spread for added richness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with grated Parmesan for an extra cheesy flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix with your favorite herbs for a burst of freshness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve as a side to your favorite sandwich or burger.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a crunchy topping on salads for added texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your Air-Fried Zucchini Chips fresh and tasty:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Air-Fried Zucchini Chips Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow chips to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store at room temperature for up to 2 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For longer freshness, refrigerate for up to a week.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing  Air-Fried Zucchini Chips</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Ensure chips are completely cooled.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Layer chips in a single layer on a baking sheet.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze until solid, then transfer to a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use within 2-3 months for best quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating  Air-Fried Zucchini Chips</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Preheat your air fryer to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat chips for 3-5 minutes until crispy.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use an oven at 350°F for 5-7 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Avoid microwaving to maintain crispiness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. How do you make zucchini chips crispy in the air fryer?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make zucchini chips crispy in the air fryer, start by slicing the zucchini thinly, ideally about 1/4 inch thick. Pat the slices dry with a paper towel to remove excess moisture, which can lead to sogginess. Toss the slices in a light coating of oil and your favorite seasonings, then arrange them in a single layer in the air fryer basket. Cooking them at a higher temperature, around 400°F, for about 10-15 minutes, flipping halfway through, will help achieve that perfect crispiness!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How do I get my chips crispy in the air fryer?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To ensure your chips come out crispy in the air fryer, make sure not to overcrowd the basket. This allows hot air to circulate freely around each chip. Additionally, using a light spray of oil can help them crisp up nicely. Experimenting with different cooking times and temperatures can also help you find the perfect balance for your air fryer model!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How to fry zucchini without it getting soggy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To fry zucchini without it getting soggy, it&#8217;s essential to slice it thinly and remove as much moisture as possible. You can sprinkle the slices with salt and let them sit for about 15-20 minutes to draw out excess water, then pat them dry. Using a light coating of oil and cooking at a high temperature will also help keep them crispy!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What&#8217;s the best oil for air fryer zucchini chips?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best oil for air fryer zucchini chips is one with a high smoke point, such as avocado oil or canola oil. These oils not only help achieve a crispy texture but also add a subtle flavor without overpowering the zucchini. Olive oil is also a great option, but be mindful of its lower smoke point if cooking at higher temperatures!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to crunch your way to happiness with these Crispy Air-Fried Zucchini Chips! They’re not just a snack; they’re a delightful trip down memory lane. Simple to make and oh-so-rewarding, these chips are perfect for sharing or savoring all by yourself. So grab your zucchini and let the air fryer work its magic—your taste buds will thank you!</p>\n",
